            <ArticleTitle>Usefulness of the SafeCut Dual Wire PTCA catheter for the treatment of calcified lesions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E254-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Calcified lesions are a cause of stent underexpansion, which significantly increases the subsequent risks of restenosis and stent thrombosis, even when drug-eluting stents are used. In this report, we describe how a novel balloon catheter, the SafeCut Dual Wire percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty catheter, enabled adequate dilatation in a calcified lesion that was unresponsive to conventional balloon catheters.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
